WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.110
Hey Thoughty2 Here,

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:07.840
The 30th US president Calvin Coolidge liked
to have his head rubbed with petroleum jelly

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.830
whilst eating his breakfast and Abraham Lincoln
was also a licensed bartender.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:23.340
But how do you become president of the United
States?

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.650
There are only three official pre-requisites
to becoming president:

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.920
You must have been born in the United States
of America.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:37.010
You must have lived in America for 14 years
and you must be at least 35 years of age.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:42.950
But even if you fit all three of these requirements,
there are a bunch of unofficial rules to become

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:43.950
president.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.059
Such as:

00:00:45.059 --> 00:00:46.059
Be Male.

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:50.100
There has never been a Female president of
the US.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.260
Don't have a serious criminal record.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.460
George W. Bush had a DUI conviction in 1976.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.840
But do you really think people are going to
vote for an armed robber?

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.110
Don't be fat.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:08.880
There have only been five presidents who were
technically obese, the largest of these was

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.889
27th president, William Howard Taft, who weighed
in at 335 pounds.

00:01:14.889 --> 00:01:20.229
But since the days of TV, there hasn't been
a single obese president.

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:21.380
Be straight.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.420
The US public has never elected an openly
gay president.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:30.979
The president with the strongest evidence
of being homosexual was 15th president James

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:31.979
Buchanan.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:33.560
Be a devout Christian.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:42.359
76% of Americans are Christians and 92% believe
in a higher power so don't think you're getting

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:44.459
in if you're an atheist, or any other religion.

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:46.319
Be tall and handsome.

00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:53.359
In approximately 75% of elections the taller
and better-looking candidate wins.

00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:58.560
You're not allowed to sweat or make the American
public aware that you have any normal bodily

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.859
functions whatsoever.

00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:05.159
During the infamous 1960, Kennedy vs Nixon
debates.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:10.719
Kennedy was a natural on camera whereas a
more timid Nixon, having just come off the

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:14.739
flu, started to sweat profusely under the
hot studio lights.

00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:21.760
Kennedy later won the vote 49.7% to 49.5%.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:27.239
Polls revealed that more than half of all
voters had been influenced by the debates.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:35.480
And finally, don't claim to have invented
the internet, in 2000 Al Gore lost the presidential

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:41.400
election partially because, whilst ticking
off a list of accomplishments he let slip

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:48.030
"During my service in the United States Congress,
I took initiative in creating the Internet".

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.810
So what's the lesson here?

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:55.780
If you want to be president, never say anything
which can be taken out of context or is just

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.780
plain wrong.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:02.950
Sadly, if you don't fit all of these criteria,
the US public are unlikely to vote for you.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:09.090
So you're a Straight, Law-Abiding, Thin, Tall,
Handsome, Male, American Christian.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.129
What next?

00:03:10.129 --> 00:03:17.609
Well, it also helps to be wealthy, charismatic,
confident, an exemplary public speaker, have

00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:23.549
impeccable body language, an Ivy League education,
lots and lots of wealthy friends in powerful

00:03:23.549 --> 00:03:31.010
places, European ancestry, a wife and kids,
strong debating skills and a clear perspective

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.889
on all current issues.

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:38.090
Providing you tick all the boxes, how do you
start your presidential campaign?

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:43.450
The first step is to secure a good job in
US politics or the military.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:50.790
In the last 70 years, every major party presidential
nominee has been either a sitting or former

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.389
US senator, governor, vice-president or five-star
general.

00:03:55.389 --> 00:04:01.040
Second, you need to form an exploratory committee,
the purpose of this committee is to test the

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.480
waters, raise money for your campaign and
decide if you really have what it takes to

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.909
become president.

00:04:07.909 --> 00:04:11.349
This can begin up to two years before the
election.

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:16.489
During this time if you receive significant
interest from the media, campaign strategists

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:22.830
and potential donors you can formally declare
your candidacy and launch your presidential

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:23.830
campaign.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.930
You will also need to choose a vice president
candidate.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:31.740
The third step is campaigning, this means
travelling throughout the country to gain

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.000
the support of the public for your political
party and candidacy.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:42.099
This usually involves holding rallies, participating
in debates, kissing babies, wining and dining

00:04:42.099 --> 00:04:44.440
and posing for photographs.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:51.349
Like most parties, you should start your campaigning
in Iowa, New Hampshire and South Carolina,

00:04:51.349 --> 00:04:57.220
because these states hold the first contests
of the campaign in January before the elections.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.039
So good performance here can make or break
your campaign.

00:05:01.039 --> 00:05:04.729
You will also need to spend a lot of money
on advertising.

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:10.810
Barack Obama's party spent $1.123 billion
during his campaign.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:16.169
In the final weeks before the elections, the
contenders focus their efforts on the so-called

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:21.780
"battleground" states, where the electorate
is more or less evenly divided and hence the

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.400
outcome is uncertain.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:30.150
In these key remaining states, campaign volunteers
and paid staff furiously work the telephones

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:34.630
and go door to door to win support for their
party.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:38.740
Finally it's time for the elections, or the
"Popular Vote".

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:44.740
In America this is always held on the first
Tuesday after the first Monday in November.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.419
Every 4 years.

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:52.280
Voters from every state vote for their favourable
president and vice president candidates.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.139
But voters aren't actually voting directly
for their chosen candidate.

00:05:57.139 --> 00:06:02.810
They are actually voting for "electors", who
are pledged to a specific candidate and are

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:09.259
expected to, but don't always, vote for that
candidate in a second, final election.

00:06:09.259 --> 00:06:12.409
This process is known as the "Electoral College".

00:06:12.409 --> 00:06:18.909
Each state has a certain number of electors
in the college, based on the size of its population.

00:06:18.909 --> 00:06:24.069
In total there are 538 electors in the electoral
college.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:29.599
Because of this system, a candidate can become
president without winning the popular vote,

00:06:29.599 --> 00:06:33.509
if the chosen electors don't vote as expected.

00:06:33.509 --> 00:06:39.289
This happened in the 2000 George W. Bush vs.
Al Gore election.

00:06:39.289 --> 00:06:43.230
Congratulations, you've passed the world's
hardest job interview.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:48.229
For all your efforts you're now a prisoner
of the White House, unable to even walk across

00:06:48.229 --> 00:06:54.789
the street without a legion of Secret Service
agents and a group of aides tagging along.

00:06:54.789 --> 00:07:00.419
You will have to endure 24/7 scrutiny of your
every word and action.

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:05.360
And work 12 hour days where your schedule
is planned to the minute.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:11.139
Don't forget the ongoing and relentless assault
from hostile news and media and opposition

00:07:11.139 --> 00:07:15.050
parties dedicated to impeding your every move.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:20.669
Only difficult decisions will reach your desk,
the easy ones are all taken care of at lower

00:07:20.669 --> 00:07:23.360
levels of your administration.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.379
What's your reward for all this?

00:07:25.379 --> 00:07:33.039
Well you get an annual salary of $400,000
per year, plus an annual expense, travel and

00:07:33.039 --> 00:07:40.830
entertainment account, these bonuses bring
your total salary to $550,000 per year.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:47.330
Which seems like a lot, but is actually a
rather measly wage compared to your responsibilities.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:51.849
Most presidents could earn a lot more if they
worked in the private sector.

00:07:51.849 --> 00:07:55.389
So what's the real reward for all your hardships?

00:07:55.389 --> 00:08:01.039
You will go down in the history books alongside
George Washington and you get to put your

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:13.009
personal stamp on a country of 313.9 million
people, and subsequently the world.

